{"kind":"stack","id":"stk-materials","title":"Everyday materials: why we use them","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1a2b3c","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Metal"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-d","content":"A hard material that conducts heat and electricity well and is often shiny."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Why are saucepans often made of metal?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Metal conducts heat well and does not melt easily","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Metal is soft and easy to bend","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Metal lets light pass through it","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"A fair test checked which material keeps water warm longest. Which material should a pupil choose for a warm-water bottle?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Wool, which trapped the most heat in the test","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Tin foil, which let heat escape fastest","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Glass, which cracked during the test","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You are building a shelter for a camp. Which material do you choose?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Wood, because it is strong and easy to cut","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Plastic, because it is waterproof","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Wood keeps out the wind and holds up the roof well. The shelter stands firm all week."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Plastic keeps out the rain, but it bends in the wind and the roof sags."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Fair test"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-d","content":"A test where only one thing is changed at a time, so the results can be trusted."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Why are wooden table tops used in classrooms?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Wood is strong and can be sanded smooth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Wood is see-through","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Wood melts in hot sun","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which material is best for a raincoat?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Plastic, because water does not soak through it","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Paper, because it is thin and light","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Cotton, because it is see-through","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"A fair test found that a metal spoon and a plastic spoon were left in hot water. Which one became hot to hold first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"The metal spoon, because metal conducts heat quickly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"The plastic spoon, because plastic conducts heat quickly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Both at the same time, because both are spoons","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"Why are bridges often made of steel?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Steel is strong enough to hold heavy loads","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"Steel floats on water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"Steel is soft enough to bend with the traffic","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"Well done: you explored everyday materials!"},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"You can now give reasons for choosing metal, wood and plastic, based on fair tests."}],"actions":[]}}
